```","mcp__data__form_elicitation_v2_request Collect answers in a blocking native form. Execution waits for final submission even when every field is optional.

When to call
Use only when missing required source material prevents meaningful progress, the user requests a form/picker, or the user explicitly asks to wait. Finish independent work first. Otherwise continue with sensible assumptions; non-template clarifications may use request_user_input_async. Never proactively block on template selection: use a suitable default. If the user asks or accepts an offer to choose templates, use only a rich resource/resources picker, never async or plain-choice questions.

Question types
- text: free text; returns a string.
- single_select: one choice; returns its option ID.
- multi_select: several choices; returns option IDs.
- resource: one template or prior analysis; returns an offered URI.
- resources: several resources; returns offered URIs.
- files: returns file URIs; use only after upload is chosen or a referenced uploaded file is missing.

Build the form
Discover real resource choices before calling. Send independent blockers or requested choices together in display order, one question per step. Wait for submission before asking a dependent question. Set required: false for every Data intake field, including files. Follow the schema's message/title guidance. Previews are optional; follow shared/template-previews.md for thumbnails and authentic icons. Images accept HTTPS or base64 PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP/AVIF, not SVG or file URLs. Do not open duplicate input surfaces.

Results and boundaries
Returns accept with content keyed by question ID, decline, cancel, or an error. Do not reopen a cancelled form automatically or treat timeouts as default answers. A selected URI does not establish readability or edit permission; file selection does not transfer bytes. Plugin installation/sign-in use Plugin Management. This tool performs no discovery, image fetching, artifact changes, or analysis. This tool is part of plugin `Data`.

